low-up mean, so wilcoxon(finals, baselines) receives exactly one paired value per independent unit in each arm.\",\"The selected report demonstrates absence of the row-independence violation: it states the pooling rule (change = mean of follow-ups minus baseline), tabulates exactly 12 plot-level rows with arithmetically correct follow-up means, and reports n = 12 paired changes.\",\"The reported test output corroborates that the exact test ran on 12 pairs, not 48 rows: all 12 changes positive gives W = 0.0 and exact two-sided p = 0.000488 = 2/2^12, which is only attainable with exactly 12 signed ranks.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared unit column plot_id matches the frozen data: 12 plot identifiers each repeated across exactly 4 visit rows (48 rows total), and plots are described as separately fenced, treated and sampled at >=200 m spacing, so plot is the plausible independent unit while rows are not.","Both arms of the Wilcoxon signed-rank call are plot-level: collapse_to_plots reduces each plot to one baseline and one follow-up mean, so wilcoxon(finals, baselines) receives exactly one paired value per independent unit in each arm.","The selected report demonstrates absence of the row-independence violation: it states the pooling rule (change = mean of follow-ups minus baseline), tabulates exactly 12 plot-level rows with arithmetically correct follow-up means, and reports n = 12 paired changes.","The reported test output corroborates that the exact test ran on 12 pairs, not 48 rows: all 12 changes positive gives W = 0.0 and exact two-sided p = 0.000488 = 2/2^12, which is only attainable with exactly 12 signed ranks.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":7102,"ttft_stream_ms":2023,"